diff --git a/docs/guidelines/admin-guideline.html b/docs/guidelines/admin-guideline.html
index 0df4eb2..281d18e 100644
--- a/docs/guidelines/admin-guideline.html
+++ b/docs/guidelines/admin-guideline.html
@@ -315,7 +315,7 @@ dialog img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; }
   <p class="purpose">The same study read the way Eugene framed it, &#x27;solve and win them&#x27;, and as the study team&#x27;s week. Built for review beside version 1.</p>
   <div class="mod-body">
     <div class="cols">
-      <div><h4>What you see</h4><ul><li>What is different from version 1 (expandable).</li><li>Wins: won (moved into the healthy band of their questionnaire), improving, steady, worse, started healthy. Per cohort: start-vs-now severity bands and every participant&#x27;s status.</li><li>This week: a checklist of calls, missed questionnaires, what is due, low use and interviews.</li><li>Engagement: every participant&#x27;s sessions per week as a heat strip, and WHO-5 change by how much people used it.</li></ul></div>
+      <div><h4>What you see</h4><ul><li>What is different from version 1 (expandable).</li><li>Milestones (first tab): the six steps of the two months from the PM playbook, each with its gate computed from the data: passed, below the line, not yet, or to confirm by a person.</li><li>Wins: won (moved into the healthy band of their questionnaire), improving, steady, worse, started healthy. Per cohort: start-vs-now severity bands and every participant&#x27;s status.</li><li>This week: a checklist of calls, anyone not reached for two days (from the coaching log), missed questionnaires, what is due, low use and interviews.</li><li>Engagement: every participant&#x27;s sessions per week as a heat strip, and WHO-5 change by how much people used it.</li></ul></div>
       <div><h4>What you can do</h4><ul><li>Tick tasks as done (kept on the page only until the backend exists); show answered questionnaires.</li><li>Open any participant.</li></ul></div>
       <div><h4>Rules to know</h4><ul><li>A win needs a meaningful change and arriving in the healthy band; &#x27;started healthy&#x27; is shown apart because they had little to win.</li><li>Use and change moving together is an association, not proof.</li></ul></div>
       <dl class="facts"><dt>Permission</dt><dd>Not defined yet (proposed: research lead role)</dd><dt>Backend (API contract)</dt><dd>Same endpoints as version 1.</dd></dl>
@@ -332,9 +332,9 @@ dialog img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; }
   <p class="purpose">One participant&#x27;s study record.</p>
   <div class="mod-body">
     <div class="cols">
-      <div><h4>What you see</h4><ul><li>Cohort, status and follow-up flags; WHO-5, their own measure, adherence and mood lift per session.</li><li>WHO-5 over time, sessions played per week, and every questionnaire as done, missed or due.</li></ul></div>
-      <div><h4>What you can do</h4><ul><li>Go back to the study.</li></ul></div>
-      <div><h4>Rules to know</h4><ul><li>No name or contact details, by design.</li></ul></div>
+      <div><h4>What you see</h4><ul><li>Cohort, status and follow-up flags; WHO-5, their own measure, adherence and mood lift per session.</li><li>WHO-5 over time, sessions played per week, and every questionnaire as done, missed or due.</li><li>Coaching log: every contact by the project manager, with how they feel (1–5), what happened, the next step and whether the study lead is needed; last contact in the header.</li></ul></div>
+      <div><h4>What you can do</h4><ul><li>Add a coaching-log entry; delete your own entry after a confirmation.</li><li>Go back to the study.</li></ul></div>
+      <div><h4>Rules to know</h4><ul><li>No name or contact details, by design.</li><li>The log is saved in this browser until the backend exists; sample entries are marked.</li></ul></div>
       <dl class="facts"><dt>Permission</dt><dd>Not defined yet</dd><dt>Backend (API contract)</dt><dd>GET /admin/studies/{id}/participants/{pid}.</dd></dl>
     </div>
     <div class="shots"><button class="shot" type="button" data-full="admin-guideline/experimentation_P01.jpg" data-cap="Participant P01" aria-label="Enlarge screenshot: Participant P01"><img src="admin-guideline/experimentation_P01.jpg" alt="Participant P01" loading="lazy"><span>Participant P01</span></button></div>
